{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration","id":1240952,"title":"Geist as inspiration?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-31T10:54:17-07:00","id":1240952,"title":"Geist as inspiration?","content":"Less interested in direct mage/geist crossover, but it seems like Geist has a bunch of things going on that might interest Mages, from mechanics about ghosts to the way the Underworld works, and I thought I'd open up a place for discussing that for anyone interested.<br /> <br /> One of the things that's come to my attention is that there are ghosts who deal with Memories. They can be created, traded and destroyed. With Death, you can probably interact with these directly or indirectly, and it made me think they might work as a good mechanism for describing some of how Logophages work in 2e since they're not ripping things from people's heads with Mind anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T15:24:44-07:00","id":1241039,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s another thought, ghosts can create new Memories by interacting with the living. Which means that Mages have a very attractive bargaining chip they can use with ghosts even with the restriction of not being able to create the same kind of memory the same way with the same ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T15:34:22-07:00","id":1241045,"title":"","content":"I wonder what metaphysical place all those ghosts created ex nihilo by Death Masters occupy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T19:45:24-07:00","id":1241127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1241045#post1241045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what metaphysical place all those ghosts created ex nihilo by Death Masters occupy.</div> </div> </div> </div>They actually have a ghost like that mentioned in the appendix on the Absent. It\u2019s Aspiration is to live because it never got a chance too.<br /> <br /> Huh, a ghost like that though could be a really interesting plot hook. Like maybe it\u2019s designed to exploit the Underworld\u2019s nature of greedy consumption of dead things against itself, like poisoning the well. And that\u2019s just one idea.<br /> <br /> I wonder if Mages can bottle water from the Rivers.<br /> <br /> Also, I bet Mages are fairly big on collecting Mementos even if they can\u2019t access their Keys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T19:54:47-07:00","id":1241130,"title":"","content":"Ah, the Never Born. Forgot about that for a moment. <br /> <br /> There\u2019s also how Ceremonies and Krewes work for what might grab mages\u2019 interests.<br /> <br /> And of course, how the Eaters of the Dead work. There\u2019s probably a Lich or dozen out there who replicate their methods (or at least philosophy) via Supernal magic...<br /> <br /> Oh, and there\u2019s likely a mage out there whose Awakening spawned a doppelganger. <br /> <br /> And let\u2019s not forget what the Seers of the Psychopomp have to say with regards to the Underworld...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 07-31-2018, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T20:47:35-07:00","id":1241149,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, I forgot that Ceremonies can work for anyone.<br /> <br /> I suppose that Kerberoi and the Old Laws are beyond the means of normal Mages to affect via Supernal magic. Which means of course that there's space for the inevitable something that breaks those rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T21:02:51-07:00","id":1241154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1241127#post1241127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, I bet Mages are fairly big on collecting Mementos even if they can\u2019t access their Keys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I bet a conjunctive Death / Prime spell could use Mementos and access Keys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T02:00:03-07:00","id":1241207,"title":"","content":"Guardians of the Veil and Mysterium must love working with Memory reapers. The fact that Ghosts get stolen Occult knowledge doesn't hurt either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T04:02:25-07:00","id":1241236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1241154#post1241154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bet a conjunctive Death / Prime spell could use Mementos and access Keys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Word of Command (Prime \u2022) with Death \u2022.<br /> <br /> Only problem is a mage doesn't really get anything from it except the Doom Condition and unlocking Avernian Gates (which any Death focused mage can do with a spell). They might possibly gain Plasm if they prepare by using another Death spell to redirect that Plasm to a fitting container (either physical one, a Bound, or a vampire who's gotten a Plasm pool through Essentiaphagia) since they themselves can't receive Plasm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T06:22:49-07:00","id":1241275,"title":"","content":"More on Seers &amp; the Psychopomp; I can see Libertines form a joint column-krewe with Sin-Eaters pursuing Catabasis to reform the Underworld, both to prove that Human Culture really does hold magic on its own, and as a metaphorical middle finger straight to the concept of Tyranny Of Finality and Fear Of Death that is the Psychopomp.<br /> <br /> And as their opposite number, a pylon of Seers serving the Psychopomp, allied with a host of Reapers.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> Also, if all Rank 3+ ghosts are geists, then would the section detailing ghostly Rank in Mage core be wrong? They describe geists as a subset of lares etc IIRC. Maybe mages define \u201cgeist\u201d narrowly, as those who can/do make the Bargain. <br /> <br /> And what was the relation between ectoplasm created by Death magic and Plasm again? IIRC, they\u2019re the same. That has rather... interesting implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 08-01-2018, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T08:43:56-07:00","id":1241324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1241275#post1241275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if all Rank 3+ ghosts are geists, then would the section detailing ghostly Rank in Mage core be wrong? They describe geists as a subset of lares etc IIRC. Maybe mages define \u201cgeist\u201d narrowly, as those who can/do make the Bargain.</div> </div> </div> </div>That section was wrong even before the book came out. I think Dave mentioned that it's supposed to be from the perspective of mages with incomplete understanding. I think they just fudged it because they hadn't decided completely on how GtSE would be back then. Not that those two are mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1241275#post1241275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what was the relation between ectoplasm created by Death magic and Plasm again? IIRC, they\u2019re the same. That has rather... interesting implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T14:26:51-07:00","id":1241496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1241324#post1241324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That section was wrong even before the book came out. I think Dave mentioned that it's supposed to be from the perspective of mages with incomplete understanding. I think they just fudged it because they hadn't decided completely on how GtSE would be back then. Not that those two are mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay, OOC bleeding into IC. Further emphasizes how mages are ultimately observers/outsiders, compared to the \u201cnatives.\u201d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are the same. </div> </div> </div>Thought so. <br /> <br /> Mmm, Death mages really do make good allies/antagonists to the Bound and ghosts...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T22:55:28-07:00","id":1241689,"title":"","content":"Now I'm picturing a joint chronicle in which an Eater of the Dead is both the villain the krewe is trying to take down and the Mystery the cabal is trying to solve - except, of course, the mages don't necessarily think &quot;breaking down ghosts for their Plasm&quot; is the same as &quot;eating people,&quot; and thus don't quite get what the fuss is about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T23:01:00-07:00","id":1241693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1241689#post1241689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm picturing a joint chronicle in which an Eater of the Dead is both the villain the krewe is trying to take down and the Mystery the cabal is trying to solve - except, of course, the mages don't necessarily think &quot;breaking down ghosts for their Plasm&quot; is the same as &quot;eating people,&quot; and thus don't quite get what the fuss is about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could happen. You'd have to be careful of themes though. Geist obviously comes down on the side of ghosts being people. Mage is more ambiguous, it could swing either way depending on their personal views. Although frankly, in a way, Mages -know- that ghosts are people, they just have the power to not give a damn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T04:52:20-07:00","id":1241765,"title":"","content":"What was the definition of the Realms Invisible and the Lower Depths again? Or more specifically, what was it that separated them again? Because the Underworld fits the \u201cdevouring,\u201d and \u201clacking something\u201d marks pretty well, which IIRC are traits of Lower realms. At least the Shadow has positive feedback via Resonance (even though its natives are mostly hostile), and the Astral exists inside/between everyone\u2019s souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T06:26:22-07:00","id":1241795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1241765#post1241765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was the definition of the Realms Invisible and the Lower Depths again? Or more specifically, what was it that separated them again? Because the Underworld fits the \u201cdevouring,\u201d and \u201clacking something\u201d marks pretty well, which IIRC are traits of Lower realms. At least the Shadow has positive feedback via Resonance (even though its natives are mostly hostile), and the Astral exists inside/between everyone\u2019s souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iirc 1e (think it was in Summoners) stated that if the supernal realms are above the fallen world the underworld is below it, further apart from the supernal than other invisible realms. The lower depths are something even farther away... though personally I wager that the distinction becomes moot the lower you go in the underworld. In my mind its basically a gradually developing lower depth, with the autochtonous depths being a more or less normal invisible realm, though with a sort of gravity pulling away from the fallen world. as you cross more and more rivers the more alien things get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T06:31:55-07:00","id":1241798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1241795#post1241795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Iirc 1e (think it was in Summoners) stated that if the supernal realms are above the fallen world the underworld is below it, further apart from the supernal than other invisible realms. The lower depths are something even farther away... though personally I wager that the distinction becomes moot the lower you go in the underworld. In my mind its basically a gradually developing lower depth, with the autochtonous depths being a more or less normal invisible realm, though with a sort of gravity pulling away from the fallen world. as you cross more and more rivers the more alien things get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and now that I recall, Dark Eras said Hellenistic mages perceived the world(s) almost exactly as you said, with the Astral close to the Supernal and the Underworld close to the Depths. And the Shadow, being the \u201cmiddle,\u201d not seen much distinct from the Material world. Fun things to think about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T06:40:29-07:00","id":1241802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1241765#post1241765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was the definition of the Realms Invisible and the Lower Depths again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Entering a Depth is generally a one-way trip, usually because the place's signature lack is the direct undoing of visitors. There's a case to be made for the Underworld having been subverted by the introduction of entities from the Lower Depths, but the place is attached to the world through the Resonance of Death just as surely as the Shadow is connected to the world through every other kind of Resonance. (Recall that the Shadow is not where Resonance comes from, either.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T06:57:03-07:00","id":1241804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1241802#post1241802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entering a Depth is generally a one-way trip, usually because the place's signature lack is the direct undoing of visitors. There's a case to be made for the Underworld having been subverted by the introduction of entities from the Lower Depths, but the place is attached to the world through the Resonance of Death just as surely as the Shadow is connected to the world through every other kind of Resonance. (Recall that the Shadow is not where Resonance comes from, either.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm failry sure that once you go deep enough in the underworld you will arrive in a domain whose &quot;lack&quot; (perhaps in the form of specific old laws that enforce themselves) will make a return impossible/be your undoing, barring protections on a truly epic scale.<br /> <br /> edit: I'd also argue that death resonance also reaches out into the shadow. Iirc spirits of death, decay etc. are a thing of their own, wholly separate from the underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 08-02-2018, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T07:03:57-07:00","id":1241806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1241802#post1241802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entering a Depth is generally a one-way trip, usually because the place's signature lack is the direct undoing of visitors. There's a case to be made for the Underworld having been subverted by the introduction of entities from the Lower Depths, but the place is attached to the world through the Resonance of Death just as surely as the Shadow is connected to the world through every other kind of Resonance. (Recall that the Shadow is not where Resonance comes from, either.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that\u2019s right, Resonance was Supernal in origin as far as mages know it. Forgot that for a sec.<br /> <br /> Perhaps then the Lower Depths can be described as realms in Dissonance with the rest of the Fallen World. <br /> <br /> Hmm, this would mean that the Invisible Realms are otherworlds tied to the Material via Resonance. Then the Underworld is the odd one out, with the tying Resonance being almost exclusively that of Death and Memories. The latter is broad enough, but still kinda narrow compared to what the Shadow and Astral embody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T07:03:59-07:00","id":1241807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1241804#post1241804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm failry sure that once you go deep enough in the underworld you will arrive in a domain whose &quot;lack&quot; (perhaps in the form of specific old laws that enforce themselves) will make a return impossible/be your undoing, barring protections on a truly epic scale.<br /> <br /> edit: I'd also argue that death resonance also reaches out into the shadow. Iirc spirits of death, decay etc. are a thing of their own, wholly separate from the underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not how the Old Laws have ever been portrayed, but you do you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T10:02:28-07:00","id":1241891,"title":"","content":"Considering that Sin-Eaters think the Underworld is clearly in a bad state of health and has changed for the worse it's entirely possible that the Underworld used to not be so much like a Lower Depth. That does raise the question of what changed, and there could be any number of answers to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T17:48:21-07:00","id":1242156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1241891#post1241891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that Sin-Eaters think the Underworld is clearly in a bad state of health and has changed for the worse it's entirely possible that the Underworld used to not be so much like a Lower Depth. That does raise the question of what changed, and there could be any number of answers to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting that the only ephemeral beings who don't have to have Essence provided for them live in the world inside everything's soul or in the damp caves and rivers where ghosts are broken down for Essence \u2014 otherwise, pretty much every Invisible Realm that isn't sustained by its own context is minimally &quot;hungry&quot; enough that despite the lack of Essence bleed a certain amount of subsistence farming and cannibalism is necessary to remain active. The Underworld is primarily unique in its specific predation upon the dormant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T19:40:13-07:00","id":1242215,"title":"","content":"The existence of Wounds (which are Irises to the Inferno, whicj is a Lower Depth) does not make the Shadow a Lower Depth.<br /> <br /> The Underworld is heavily damaged, provably the worst-damaged Fallen World, but it's still an ephemeral realm made of an Arcanum","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T09:39:51-07:00","id":1243524,"title":"","content":"So, we know that Plasm contains Essence, and that Geists can gift Essence to Ghosts via Plasm with a 3:1 conversion rate. I'm not clear on whether this is a natural ability of Plasm, or something that relies on the metaphysical nature of Sin Eaters, though I'm guessing it's closer to the latter, or else Ghosts would just consume Plasm on their own to regain Essence without having a middleman.<br /> <br /> So, if I wanted a spell that converted Plasm to Essence at that same ratio, what would it be?<ul><li><b>Ruling</b>, because Plasm is already capable of turning into Essence? (We must assume the conversion is inherent to Plasm, and the ghost's inability to process it on their own is due to something they explicitly lack, not something that Geists have)</li> <li><b>Weaving</b>, because Plasm and Essence aren't wholly separate, but Plasm is incapable of converting on its own? (We must assume that Essence and Plasm are just different expressions of the same thing)</li> <li><b>Patterning</b>, because Plasm isn't Essence, and it's magic unique to Sin-Eaters that allows the conversion (We must assume that references to Plasm 'containing' Essence are not literal, and merely figurative references to the ability of Sin-Eaters to convert it)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T14:34:21-07:00","id":1243603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1243524#post1243524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, we know that Plasm contains Essence, and that Geists can gift Essence to Ghosts via Plasm with a 3:1 conversion rate. I'm not clear on whether this is a natural ability of Plasm, or something that relies on the metaphysical nature of Sin Eaters, though I'm guessing it's closer to the latter, or else Ghosts would just consume Plasm on their own to regain Essence without having a middleman.<br /> <br /> So, if I wanted a spell that converted Plasm to Essence at that same ratio, what would it be?<ul><li><b>Ruling</b>, because Plasm is already capable of turning into Essence? (We must assume the conversion is inherent to Plasm, and the ghost's inability to process it on their own is due to something they explicitly lack, not something that Geists have)</li> <li><b>Weaving</b>, because Plasm and Essence aren't wholly separate, but Plasm is incapable of converting on its own? (We must assume that Essence and Plasm are just different expressions of the same thing)</li> <li><b>Patterning</b>, because Plasm isn't Essence, and it's magic unique to Sin-Eaters that allows the conversion (We must assume that references to Plasm 'containing' Essence are not literal, and merely figurative references to the ability of Sin-Eaters to convert it)</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>My gut instincts say Weaving, but we\u2019ll have to read deeper into what Plasm is to be sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T20:37:34-07:00","id":1245043,"title":"","content":"I wonder if you could use Prime to safely enter a Lower Depth or to be temporarily immune to the Old Laws. Basically, you would use a Practice of Shielding in the Material to create a reality bubble, or weave and reinforce the idea of &quot;I am operating in the Material Plane&quot;. Sure, a Depth with no Prime could possibly justify it dispelling (or needing to be fed mana constantly) or a sufficiently annoyed kerberoi could break it, but it might be interesting to work with the arcane equivalent of a space suit. Maybe you could even hang the spell, fire it at a spirit in the Shadow and have them experience Essence bleed as if they had crossed the Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T21:51:12-07:00","id":1245055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1245043#post1245043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if you could use Prime to safely enter a Lower Depth or to be temporarily immune to the Old Laws. Basically, you would use a Practice of Shielding in the Material to create a reality bubble, or weave and reinforce the idea of &quot;I am operating in the Material Plane&quot;. Sure, a Depth with no Prime could possibly justify it dispelling (or needing to be fed mana constantly) or a sufficiently annoyed kerberoi could break it, but it might be interesting to work with the arcane equivalent of a space suit. Maybe you could even hang the spell, fire it at a spirit in the Shadow and have them experience Essence bleed as if they had crossed the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lower Depths and the Underworld aren't the same thing and the Old Laws are in the Underworld and may or may not exist in Lower Depths depending on if those Lower Depths have some variation of an Underworld in them and it's similarity to the Underworld which is actually the topic of this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T00:41:06-07:00","id":1245068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1245043#post1245043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Maybe you could even hang the spell, fire it at a spirit in the Shadow and have them experience Essence bleed as if they had crossed the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>That wouldn't work, as the Shadow is a real, true part of the fallen world. A &quot;reality bubble&quot; wouldn't do anything to a spirit, they are real. I could see it accelerating Essence bleed in the material with a Perfecting spell making the material more material, so to speak.<br /> <br /> As for the whole idea of wether such a shielding spell would work the awnser is a solid maybe, depending on your ST. Of course you're screwed if the lower depth you jump into lacks in Prime.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T08:28:08-07:00","id":1245116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1245055#post1245055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lower Depths and the Underworld aren't the same thing and the Old Laws are in the Underworld and may or may not exist in Lower Depths depending on if those Lower Depths have some variation of an Underworld in them and it's similarity to the Underworld which is actually the topic of this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said they were the same. I asked if that worked to protect you in a Lower Depth and if, consequently, it could be extended to other trips outside the material, such as shielding you from the Old Laws of the Underworld. I just said it in a shorter way.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I can see why it would need a more specialized Spirit effect to cause the Essence bleed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-12-2018, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T10:19:20-07:00","id":1245135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1240952-geist-as-inspiration?p=1245116#post1245116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never said they were the same. I asked if that worked to protect you in a Lower Depth and if, consequently, it could be extended to other trips outside the material, such as shielding you from the Old Laws of the Underworld. I just said it in a shorter way.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I can see why it would need a more specialized Spirit effect to cause the Essence bleed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd be about as protected as a Supernal entity that managed to force its way from the Supernal to the Fallen without being summoned and having the benefit of any of the protections that a summoner can put in place to increase the chances of their survival.<br /> <br /> Prime doesn't deal with Death or the Underworld at all except in some tangential ways such as being able to make things solid to all levels of Twilight so it's very unlikely to help you avoid Old Laws. The same goes for using Prime to try and interfere with spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}